# Settings › Home server › Services and AI (docs/HOME-SERVER.md): AI pictures, ComfyUI on this PC's graphics card, as you.
# ComfyUI isn't in the image: Settings installs it only when you ask (hearth-home-server pictures-install: its release
# tag, the commit checked, a venv, PyTorch's CUDA 12.8 builds) into ~/ComfyUI, or adopts the one you made yourself.
# It listens on 127.0.0.1 and this PC's Tailscale address only (hearth-home-server ai-run), and its port is in
# Hearth's Tailscale-only firewall rule while it's on. No install section: started only by its timer (a minute after you
# sign in, enabled only while it's on) or by Settings; Light mode stops it while you play. Never part of starting the
# PC, the session or Game Mode: with no ComfyUI it doesn't start at all.
[Unit]
Description=Hearth home server: AI pictures (ComfyUI)
ConditionPathExists=%h/ComfyUI/main.py
ConditionPathExists=%h/ComfyUI/venv/bin/python
After=network.target

[Service]
ExecStart=/usr/bin/python3 /usr/share/nimbus/desktop/shell/hearth-home-server ai-run comfyui
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=30
Nice=5
TimeoutStopSec=30
